From 82c453a9c739d3da9cd74126e106227c1948e747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:11:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): pull board_error records the failed HTTP
 attempt's budget/elapsed [daveey]

A dispatch-tick feed pull timeout fanned out as stage=pull, transport=timeout with no timing (only
reserve/repin were instrumented), so a starved page-2 GET looked like a slow page-1 GET.

Hub now stamps each FAILED HTTP attempt (kept-alive and urlopen paths) with raw (budget_s, elapsed_s):
budget left on the shared deadline when THAT attempt started, and its own time to fail. A stale-socket
GET retry restarts the clock; budget exhausted before an attempt stamps nothing. The stamp lives in a
new sibling kanban_sync_client_attempt (client never imports the queue layer). record_pull_error reads
it via queue.attempt_timing using the same _ms rounding/clamping as reserve/repin; absent, malformed or
non-finite values are omitted and never mask the error.

Diagnostics only: exception classes, OSError/URLError wrapping, attempts, deadlines, POST no-replay,
event+comment fanout/dedupe and reserve/repin timing are unchanged. No timeout or suppression change.
(Removed an unused `# noqa: A002` in the RED test file for ruff RUF100; no assertion touched.)

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pull_attempt_timing.py RED (2 failed: no budget_ms) -> GREEN;
new test_kanban_pull_attempt_timing_edges.py (23) covers stale-GET retry timing, POST no-replay,
exhausted-before-retry, no-deadline, urlopen path, absent/malformed/non-finite stamps, dedupe.
Mutants on each added condition killed. Focused suite 200 passed; scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
